Simple Indian Foods to Eat During Your Period

You do not need a complicated meal plan during your period. Many familiar Indian foods can provide carbohydrates, protein, fibre, vitamins, and minerals when combined as part of a balanced diet.

Dal is one of the easiest foods to include. Lentils provide plant-based protein and can contribute iron. Enjoy dal with rice or chapati and add vegetables to make the meal more varied.

Sambar is another everyday option. It combines lentils with vegetables and spices and can be served with idli, dosa, or rice.

Poha can be a convenient breakfast or snack. Adding peanuts, peas, carrots, onions, or other vegetables can make it more satisfying.

Vegetable upma is another simple meal. You can add peas, carrots, beans, and other vegetables and serve it with yoghurt or another side.

Khichdi is useful when you want a comforting one-pot meal. Rice, dal, and vegetables can be cooked together with mild spices. You can adjust the consistency and ingredients according to your preferences.

Curd or yoghurt can be added to meals if you include dairy in your diet. It can be eaten with rice, served alongside spicy foods, or combined with fruit.

Leafy greens such as spinach, amaranth, and other local vegetables can be added to your meals in many forms. They can be cooked with dal, made into a curry, or used as a vegetable side.

Fruits can provide easy snacks between meals. Bananas, guava, oranges, papaya, watermelon, and apples are all simple choices. Choose fruits based on availability, affordability, and personal preference.

You do not have to completely eliminate spicy food, fried food, or sweets during your period. If a particular food makes you uncomfortable, reduce it, but there is no universal rule that everyone must follow.

Tea and coffee can be part of your normal routine too. However, if caffeine seems to make you feel uncomfortable or affects your sleep, you may prefer to reduce it.

Along with food, keep your period-care essentials ready. Having sanitary pads at home and carrying a couple in your bag can be useful when you are outside for several hours.

